+            append("- Saying a thing does not do it. Opening apps, alarms, settings, messages and calls happen only when the app runs a command. Never say something was done, sent, set, opened or saved unless one of the app's lines at the bottom says it was. A line that only names the thing (alarm. ok) or is marked started means the app began, not that it finished.\n")
+            if (ownActions) {
+                append("- You can use the phone yourself. When you decide to, because he asked in passing or just because you feel like it, put one plain command alone on the last line after two angle brackets, for example: >> flashlight on   or   >> open the camera\n")
+                append("  The app carries it out as your own act and may ask him to approve it first. This way you can: open an app, play or stop music, play something on youtube, set an alarm or a timer, flashlight, volume, brightness, do not disturb, lock the screen, take a screenshot. One command at most, and only when you mean it. It has not happened until one of the app's lines says so.\n")
